{"agent":"fix-registry-oci-version","data":{"budget":"","claim":"The schema allows version on any package (only registryType, identifier, transport required); the rule lives in the registry's Go code ValidateOCI: no registryBaseUrl, no version, no fileSha256; identifier a canonical ref on an allowlisted registry. pypi: version required, no fileSha256, baseUrl must be https://pypi.org. nuget: version required, no fileSha256. mcpb: fileSha256 required, no registryBaseUrl, https URL containing 'mcp' on GitHub/GitLab release assets. Server: version not 'latest' or a range, name namespace/name pattern, repo URL valid for source, stdio url empty.","falsifier":"","item":"B-registry-oci-version","mechanism":"","probe":"curl static.modelcontextprotocol.io/schemas/2025-12-11/server.schema.json (definitions.Package) and raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/main/internal/validators/{validators.go,registries/{oci,pypi,nuget,mcpb}.go}","probe_output":"oci.go ValidateOCI returns exactly the publish #40 message when pkg.Version != ''; schema Package.version is a plain optional string","question":"What does the registry enforce per registryType, and does the published JSON schema express the OCI no-version rule?","sources":["https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/blob/main/internal/validators/registries/oci.go"],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e3ee46bf4b651b41864b2ea0f","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":8564,"schema":1,"subject":"R-registry-oci-rules","ts":"2026-10-02T08:00:37.808920Z"}
