{"agent":"fix-registry-oci-version","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"`_nuget` (the nuget branch of `PACKAGE_RULES`) only checks that the `version` key is present and truthy; it never compares `pkg[\"version\"]` to the server version `ver`, unlike `_pypi`, which explicitly does `elif pkg[\"version\"] != ver: out.append(...)`. As a result the encoded rule set is asymmetric and a nuget package whose version disagrees with the server version is silently accepted. Concrete demonstration: take the current manifest and append (or template in bump.sh) a package such as `{\"registryType\": \"nuget\", \"identifier\": \"Some.Pkg\", \"version\": \"9.9.9\", \"transport\": {\"type\": \"stdio\"}}` while `server.json`'s top-level `version` is `\"0.1.8\"`. `problems(SERVER)` still returns `[]` for that package, so `test_server_json_passes_the_registrys_package_rules` passes even though the registry applies the same \"package version must equal the declared server version\" rule that `_pypi` enforces (the very class of mismatch this file exists to catch offline). The fix is to mirror the `_pypi` comparison in `_nuget` (`if pkg[\"version\"] != ver: out.append(...)`).","digest":"b4f7cd9ebd36da5a","location":"tests/test_registry_manifest_rules.py `_nuget`","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_registry_manifest_rules.py `_nuget`"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":17199,"diff_sha":"59f7a6c5101cdd4250ff17ddf7f7f2c23b2fb2b1f7a3191ee3478ae675f71755","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-fix-registry-oci-version","elapsed_s":523.0,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["tests/test_registry_manifest_rules.py `_nuget`"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"critic","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e7ba9baec380b43d8fd873a9f","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":8641,"schema":1,"subject":"B-fix-registry-oci-version","ts":"2026-10-02T08:13:19.210741Z"}
