{"agent":"fix-registry-oci-version","data":{"digest":"b4f7cd9ebd36da5a","finding":1,"gate":"critic","location":"tests/test_registry_manifest_rules.py `_nuget`","probe":"curl raw nuget.go (modelcontextprotocol/registry main) | grep -n -i 'serverVersion|ServerVersion' -> no output; ValidateNuGet only requires pkg.Version non-empty and looks that exact version up on NuGet. pypi.go likewise only requires it exist. The pypi==server version check in this test is ddflow's own release invariant (test_packaging already asserts it), not a registry rule, and a nuget package may legitimately version independently. ddflow ships no nuget package.","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_registry_manifest_rules.py `_nuget`","verdict":"refuted"},"id":"e45839f62b9e223018e367ec1","kind":"review.triaged","lamport":8658,"schema":1,"subject":"B-fix-registry-oci-version","ts":"2026-10-02T08:15:34.488191Z"}
